#: {{ux|en|Take off your '''muddy''' boots before you come inside.}}
# Of [[water#Noun|water]] or some other [[liquid#Noun|liquid]]: [[contain]]ing mud or {{lb|en|by extension}} other [[sediment#Noun|sediment]] in [[suspension]]; [[cloudy]], [[turbid]].
#: {{ux|en|The previously limpid water was now '''muddy''' as a result of the struggle between the alligator and the wild boar.}}
# [[have#Verb|Having]] the [[characteristic#Noun|characteristics]] of mud, especially in [[colour#Noun|colour]] or [[taste#Noun|taste]].
# {{lb|en|euphemistic}} [[soil#Verb|Soiled]] with [[feces]].
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Of an [[animal]] or [[plant#Noun|plant]]: [[grow#Verb|growing]] or [[live#Verb|living]] in mud.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}}
## Not [[clear#Adjective|clear]].
### Of a colour: not [[bright#Adjective|bright]]: [[dirty#Adjective|dirty]], [[dull#Adjective|dull]].
### Of an [[image#Noun|image]]: [[blurry]] or [[dim#Adjective|dim]].
### Of [[light#Noun|light]]: cloudy, [[opaque#Adjective|opaque]].
### Of [[sound#Noun|sound]] (especially during [[performance]], [[recording#Noun|recording]], or [[playback]]): [[indistinct]], [[muffled#Adjective|muffled]].
###: {{ux|en|The television picture is decent, but the sound is '''muddy'''.}}
### Of [[speech#Noun|speech]], [[thinking#Noun|thinking]], or [[writing#Noun|writing]]: [[ambiguous]] or [[vague#Adjective|vague]]; or [[confused#Adjective|confused]], [[incoherent]], or [[mixed-up]]; also, [[poorly]] [[express#Verb|expressed]].
